WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.860
A Sikh couple have tried
for a child for a long time.

2
00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:06.290
Their doctor offers IVF.

3
00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:09.380
Eggs are fertilised by
sperm in a laboratory.

4
00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:12.280
Then an embryo is placed in the womb.

5
00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:15.550
The Gurus lived centuries
before any of this.

6
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:19.590
So for a Sikh couple, is
IVF a gift of science,

7
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:22.380
or a step outside God's will?

8
00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:26.030
In this mission, you'll meet Sikh
ideas that bear on the question,

9
00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:30.360
such as hukam: God's will,
running through all of life.

10
00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:34.490
Then you'll compare three scholars,
two Sikhs and one outsider,

11
00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:36.240
and map the arguments.

12
00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:41.090
Your mission: find out how Sikh
teaching can answer the IVF question.
